[meta]
lang: en
title: OireMark conformance tests: Escaping
[/meta]

h1. Escaping

Tests for Section 6 of the specification.

h2. Punctuation Escapes

h3. Escaped formatting markers are text {#escaping-markers}
[code om]
\*not bold\*
[/code]
[code html]
<p>*not bold*</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped brackets are text {#escaping-brackets}
[code om]
\[not a tag\]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>[not a tag]</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped backslash {#escaping-backslash}
[code om]
This is a backslash: \\
[/code]
[code html]
<p>This is a backslash: \</p>
[/code]

h3. Every ASCII punctuation character can be escaped {#escaping-all-punctuation}
[code om]
\!\"\#\$\%\&\'\(\)\*\+\,\-\.\/\:\;\<\=\>\?\@\[\\\]\^\_\`\{\|\}\~
[/code]
[code html]
<p>!"#$%&amp;'()*+,-./:;&lt;=&gt;?@[\]^_`{|}~</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped underscore is a literal underscore {#escaping-underscore}
[code om]
\_not italic\_ and snake\_case
[/code]
[code html]
<p>_not italic_ and snake_case</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped marker inside formatted text {#escaping-inside-formatting}
[code om]
*a \* b*
[/code]
[code html]
<p><strong>a * b</strong></p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped backslash before a marker leaves the marker active {#escaping-double-backslash}
[code om]
\\*bold*
[/code]
[code html]
<p>\<strong>bold</strong></p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped bracket inside link text {#escaping-link-text}
[code om]
[a \] b]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com">a ] b</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped opening bracket prevents a link {#escaping-no-link}
[code om]
\[text]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p>[text]:https://example.com</p>
[/code]

h2. Escaping Line-Start Markers

h3. Escaped dot after a number is not a list {#escaping-numbered}
[code om]
1984\. A good year.
[/code]
[code html]
<p>1984. A good year.</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped hash is not a list {#escaping-hash}
[code om]
\# Not a list item
[/code]
[code html]
<p># Not a list item</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped asterisk is not a list {#escaping-asterisk-list}
[code om]
\* Not a list item
[/code]
[code html]
<p>* Not a list item</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped hyphen is not a list {#escaping-hyphen-list}
[code om]
\- Not a list item
[/code]
[code html]
<p>- Not a list item</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped hyphens are not a horizontal rule {#escaping-rule}
[code om]
\-\-\-
[/code]
[code html]
<p>---</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped greater-than is not a quote {#escaping-quote}
[code om]
\> Not a quote
[/code]
[code html]
<p>&gt; Not a quote</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped pipe is not a table {#escaping-table}
[code om]
\| Not a table |
[/code]
[code html]
<p>| Not a table |</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped semicolon is not a term {#escaping-term}
[code om]
\; Not a term
[/code]
[code html]
<p>; Not a term</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped colon is not a definition {#escaping-definition}
[code om]
\: Not a definition
[/code]
[code html]
<p>: Not a definition</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped block tag at line start is text {#escaping-block-tag}
[code om]
\[note]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>[note]</p>
[/code]

h2. Non-Breaking Space

h3. Backslash and space make a non-breaking space {#escaping-nbsp}
[code om]
10\ 000
[/code]
[code html]
<p>10&nbsp;000</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped space is kept in a table cell {#escaping-nbsp-table-cell}
[code om]
| a | \ |
[/code]
[code html]
<table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>a</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
[/code]

h3. Escaped space next to an ordinary space {#escaping-nbsp-plus-space}
[code om]
a\  b
[/code]
[code html]
<p>a&nbsp; b</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped space at the end of a line leaves a backslash {#escaping-nbsp-end-of-line}
[code hex]
61 5C 20 0A 62
[/code]
[code html]
<p>a\<br>b</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped space at the end of the document leaves a backslash {#escaping-nbsp-end-of-document}
[code hex]
31 30 5C 20
[/code]
[code html]
<p>10\</p>
[/code]

h3. A typed non-breaking space is preserved {#escaping-nbsp-literal}
[code hex]
31 30 C2 A0 30 30 30
[/code]
[code html]
<p>10&nbsp;000</p>
[/code]

h2. Other Backslashes

h3. Backslash before a letter is literal {#escaping-letter}
[code om]
\n and \t are not newlines or tabs
[/code]
[code html]
<p>\n and \t are not newlines or tabs</p>
[/code]

h3. Backslash before a digit is literal {#escaping-digit}
[code om]
\5
[/code]
[code html]
<p>\5</p>
[/code]

h3. Backslash before a non-ASCII character is literal {#escaping-non-ascii}
[code om]
\я
[/code]
[code html]
<p>\я</p>
[/code]

h3. Backslashes in a Windows path are literal {#escaping-path}
[code om]
C:\Users\Public
[/code]
[code html]
<p>C:\Users\Public</p>
[/code]

h3. Backslash at the end of a line is literal {#escaping-end-of-line}
[code om]
end\
next
[/code]
[code html]
<p>end\<br>
next</p>
[/code]

h3. Backslash at the end of the document is literal {#escaping-end-of-document}
[code om]
end\
[/code]
[code html]
<p>end\</p>
[/code]

h2. Where Escapes Do Not Apply

h3. No escapes in code spans {#escaping-code-span}
[code om]
`\*`
[/code]
[code html]
<p><code>\*</code></p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped backtick cannot open a code span {#escaping-backtick}
[code om]
\`not code`
[/code]
[code html]
<p>`not code`</p>
[/code]

h3. No escapes in code blocks {#escaping-code-block}
```om
[code]
\*x\*
[/code]
```
[code html]
<pre><code>\*x\*
</code></pre>
[/code]

h3. No escapes in URLs {#escaping-url}
[code om]
[link]:https://example.com/a\_b
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/a\_b">link</a></p>
[/code]
